, copy that spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.', 'Whenever you draw a card, Burlfist Oak gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever you draw a card, put a +1/+1 counter on Lorescale Coatl.', 'Whenever you draw a card, you may pay {1}. When you do, you may tap or untap target creature.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, Mystic Skyfish gains flying until end of turn.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, create a 2/2 green Cat creature token.\\n{4}{G}{G}: Until end of turn, creatures you control have base power and toughness X/X, where X is the number of cards in your hand.', 'Whenever you gain life, target opponent loses that much life.\\n{3}{B}{B}: Creatures you control gain lifelink until end of turn.', 'Whenever you sacrifice a permanent, Havoc Jester deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Wildwood Scourge enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\nWhenever one or more +1/+1 counters are put on another non-Hydra creature you control, put a +1/+1 counter on Wildwood Scourge.', 'Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', 'You draw two cards and each opponent discards two cards. Each player loses 2 life.', 'You gain 3 life.\\nDraw a card.', 'You gain 4 life. If a creature died this turn, you gain 8 life instead.', "You may activate loyalty abilities of Teferi, Master of Time on any player's turn any time you could cast an instant.\\n[+1]: Draw a card, then discard a card.\\n[−3]: Target creature you don't control phases out. (Treat it and anything attached to it as though they don't exist until its controller's next turn.)\\n[−10]: Take two extra turns after this one.", 'You may play two additional lands on each of your turns.', 'You may spend mana as though it were mana of any color.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}{C}{C}{C}.\\n{5}, {T}: Draw a card for each color among permanents you control.', 'Zombies you control get +1/+0.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, if a creature died this turn, you may pay {1}{B}. If you do, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', "[+1]: Chandra, Flame's Catalyst deals 3 damage to each opponent.\\n[−2]: You may cast target red instant or sorcery card from your graveyard. If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\\n[−8]: Discard your hand, then draw seven cards. Until end of turn, you may cast spells from your hand without paying their mana costs.", '[+1]: Discard your hand, then exile the top three cards of your library. Until end of turn, you may play cards exiled this way.\\n[+1]: Chandra, Heart of Fire deals 2 damage to any target.\\n[−9]: Search your graveyard and library for any number of red instant and/or sorcery cards, exile them, then shuffle. You may cast them this turn. Add six {R}.', "[+1]: Draw a card.\\n[−3]: Put target creature on top of its owner's library.\\n[−8]: Each creature target opponent controls phases out. Until the end of your next turn, they can't phase in. (Treat them and anything attached to them as though they don't exist.)", '[+1]: Each player discards a card. Each opponent who can\'t loses 3 life.\\n[−3]: Target creature gets -X/-X until end of turn, where X is the number of cards in your graveyard.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of combat on your turn, put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. It gains haste."', '[+1]: Put a +1/+1 counter on up to one target creature. It gains indestructible until end of turn.\\n[−2]: Whenever one or more nontoken creatures attack this turn, create that many 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens that are tapped and attacking.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of combat on your turn, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token, then put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control."', '[+1]: Put a +1/+1 counter on up to one target creature. It gains vigilance until end of turn.\\n[−1]: Whenever a creature attacks this turn, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\n[−6]: Creatures you control get +2/+2 and gain flying until end of turn.', '[+1]: Return up to one target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n[−3]: Destroy target creature. Its controller loses 2 life.\\n[−7]: Target opponent loses 2 life for each creature card in their graveyard.', '[+1]: Reveal the top card of your library. If it\'s a creature card, put it into your hand. Otherwise, put it on the bottom of your library.\\n[−2]: Target creature you control deals damage equal to its power to another target creature.\\n[−7]: Until end of turn, creatures you control gain "You may have this creature assign its combat damage as though it weren\'t blocked."', '[+1]: Up to one target creature gets +3/+3 and gains trample until end of turn.\\n[−2]: Create a 3/3 green Beast creature token. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, put a loyalty counter on Garruk, Unleashed.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of your end step, you may search your library for a creature card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle."', "[+2]: Ugin, the Spirit Dragon deals 3 damage to any target.\\n[−X]: Exile each permanent with mana value X or less that's one or more colors.\\n[−10]: You gain 7 life, draw seven cards, then put up to seven permanent cards from your hand onto the battlefield.", '{1}, Discard a land card or Shrine card: Sanctum of Shattered Heights deals X damage to target creature or planeswalker, where X is the number of Shrines you control.', '{1}, Sacrifice Thrashing Brontodon: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', '{1}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain 1 life and draw a card.', '{1}{B}, {T}: Each opponent loses 2 life. Activate only if a creature died this turn.', '{1}{R}: Igneous Cur gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', '{1}{U}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{1}{W}, {T}: Tap target creature. Activate only if you control a creature with flying.', '{2}: Add one mana of any color.', '{2}: Put target card from your graveyard on the bottom of your library.', '{2}{U}: Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', '{4}, {T}, Sacrifice Silent Dart: It deals 3 damage to target creature.', '{5}{W}: Tap target creature. This ability costs {1} less to activate for each Shrine you control.', '{G}: Exile target card from a graveyard. If it was a creature card, put a +1/+1 counter on Scavenging Ooze and you gain 1 life.', '{T}, Pay 3 life: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, you gain 6 life.', '{T}, Put a page counter on Mazemind Tome: Scry 1.\\n{2}, {T}, Put a page counter on Mazemind Tome: Draw a card.\\nWhen there are four or more page counters on Mazemind Tome, exile it. If you do, you gain 4 life.', '{T}, Sacrifice Fabled Passage: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle. Then if you control four or more lands, untap that land.', "{T}, Sacrifice Liliana's Steward: Target opponent discards a card. Activate only as a sorcery.", "{T}, Sacrifice Tormod's Crypt: Exile target player's graveyard.", '{T}: Add {C}. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target Bird, Cat, Dog, Goat, Ox, or Snake.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {G} for each creature with power 4 or greater you control.\\n{7}{R}: Leafkin Avenger deals damage equal to its power to target player or planeswalker.', "{T}: Chandra's Magmutt deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.", '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.\\n{2}{U}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Obsessive Stitcher: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', '{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature with a +1/+1 counter on it.\\n{4}{W}{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.']
flavor: ['"A potion is no substitute for a skilled surgeon, but it will hold your bits in."\\n—Torricks, battlefield medic', '"All are welcome in the angels\' light."', '"All peoples treasure a place where the weary traveler may drink in peace."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"All right. Warm-ups are over."', '"And if I\'m lying," he began . . .', '"Another village, another angry mob. Why do I even bother unpacking?"', '"As long as we survive, we can rebuild."\\n—Basri Ket', '"As the sky opened up, we ran for shelter. Halfway there I came to the sudden realization that, already soaked, there might be more to gain from experiencing the rain than running from it."', '"Basri has shown me the way forward, and I will follow."', '"Be glad the griffin set you back on your feet when it was done with you. My goat wasn\'t so lucky."\\n—Arram, goatherd', '"Come and listen. I\'ll tell you the story of a nation lost to time, and of the man who caused it."', '"Cruelty? No. This is necessity."\\n—Kaervek', '"Defy me and I will burn the flesh from your bones. Betray me and I will steal the breath from your lungs."', '"Drink from the vein? How provincial."\\n—Lord Duchorvin', '"Even the rats refuse to set foot inside. I fear to think what might be waiting in there."\\n—Gravedigger\'s journal', '"Fear is a rational response, but waiting won\'t make it any easier. Just jump!"', '"Feeding a normal army is a problem of logistics. With zombies, it is an asset. Feeding is why they fight. Feeding is why they are feared."\\n—Jadar, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"Fine, you know more than me. But do you have to be such a show-off about it?"\\n—Chandra Nalaar, to Teferi', '"First, the darkness fell. Terror came next. After that, only despair remained."\\n—*The Tragedy of Morein*', '"From a great bonfire at the dawn of time, the first Gruul kindled their rage. The same flame burns in you."\\n—Kroshkar, Gruul shaman', '"Gilded with gold from a dragon\'s trove, it is! And etched with the image of the dragon I slew to take it."', '"Humans bring nothing but suffering and deceit. They are not welcome in my forest."', '"I decide what stands in my way."', '"I do not miss Jukai Forest. It is not my home. My home is Kamigawa, its people my family. Wherever I set my pack and rest my head, I am home."', '"I don\'t know that I\'ll win every fight. But I have faith, and that\'s carried me this far."', '"I don\'t think they\'ll appreciate my . . . adjustments."\\n—Karavin, renegade saboteur', '"I have faith in your potential."', '"I hope the idiot who introduced these creatures to the jungle was their first meal."\\n—Opar, veteran guide', '"I look to the heavens for hope, but you will kneel."', '"I love those who are eager to serve."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"I offered to pay him to do the job, but he refused. So I took matters into my own hands."\\n—Tahim, the Puppetmaster', '"I sang of storms, there came a squall. I sang of waves, the seas grew tall. I sang of love, but no voice called."', '"I sing of benevolence and mercy, of golden wings bringing comfort to the meek and downtrodden."', '"I specialize in missing manuscripts, pilfered poetry, and lifted letters."', '"I think Chandra just wanted something to blame random scorch marks on."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"I welcome the use of even the foulest magic if it will rid us of the monstrosities that plague our world."\\n—Munda, ambush leader', '"I\'d like to introduce you to the new and improved me."', '"I\'d rather go out in a blaze of glory than fade away and be forgotten."', '"I\'ll make ice chimes of your bones."', '"I\'ve been carrying a sword since before you were born. I wouldn\'t give up my oath for all the peace and comfort in the world."', '"If it wasn\'t a blackened, stinking, melted abomination before, it certainly is now."\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"If you believe the God-Pharaoh tests you, charge with me to prove yourself. If you believe he betrayed us all, join with me to fight for tomorrow!"\\n—Samut, former Tah-crop initiate', '"In this world, it\'s kill or be killed. I\'d rather not be the latter."', '"Is it purebred? No, but it\'s pure fire."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"It certainly takes after its master: big and brutish, and you can smell it from a mile away."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"It\'s contemplative, resourceful, and original. Everything else aside, it\'s the perfect student."\\n—Naban, dean of iteration', '"Just a nibble for now. I wouldn\'t want to ruin my appetite."', '"Let\'s lure the drakes to the webs over the Samok Stand. Keep the spiders content."\\n—Aurelia', '"My falcons are family, as much as any other member of my clan."', '"My family was saved thanks to a single Boros soldier. It\'s why I joined the Legion. I will be the protector now."', '"My lance was once wielded by Venerable Tarrian. In his name and by his might, I cast you down!"', '"My roots are ash, my heart a smoldering ember. What I could not protect, I will avenge."', '"Nature is not always gentle or kind, but all life begets life."\\n—Marwyn of Llanowar', '"Never underestimate the ability of natural forces to adapt to unnatural influences."\\n—Molimo, maro-sorcerer', '"Next time, try something more appropriate for your skill level."\\n—Barrin, Tolarian archmage', '"Nicely done, Jace. You always were good at disappearing acts."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"No owners allowed."\\n—Sanctuary sign', '"No sight is more beautiful than a clear sky."', '"Oh, don\'t be so dramatic. When your eyes bleed, and your brain leaks out your ears, then we\'ll talk about lost sanity."\\n—Braids, dementia summoner', '"On the eighth day, a blizzard hit. Supplies were lost, and morale plummeted. On the ninth day, Dover found us."\\n—*To the Summit: A Tale of Survival*', '"One day the mountain\'s fire will rise up to burn away our chains and end this age of oppression."\\n—*The Molten Prophecy*', '"Quiet in the library" soon gave way to larger concerns.', '"Remind me again, what\'s the going rate for betrayal these days?"\\n—Captain Rhenmir', '"Right now, in these first moments of creation, it is simultaneously nothing and everything."', '"Rise, knight of New Benalia."', '"Six consecutive life sentences" takes on a new meaning when necromancy is involved.', '"Some savor the hunt. I savor the kill."', '"Sometimes the only difference between a martyr and a hero is a sword."\\n—Captain Sisay, *Memoirs*', '"Soul, flesh, even eyes—none of these are strictly necessary for deadly precision."\\n—Modriss of Zargoth Fen', '"Stop locking your knees as you strike! Now stand up and try again."', '"Tarassel\'s sixth law of temporal recursion is easy to understand as long as you know the first seven."', '"The beauty of it is they never see it coming. Ever."\\n—Razzix, sparkmage', '"The best denials are simply that: a beginning and end unchanged, a dream with no memory."', '"The common folk call it the breaking of the crust or the spilling of fire. Geomancers call it target practice."\\n—Ryda, geomancer', '"The enlightenment I never found in etherium I have found traced in the coatl\'s scales."\\n—Ranalus, vedalken heretic', '"The strong eat. The weak are eaten. That\'s the way of things."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"The will to fight and act as one is not limited to a single world. Oketra\'s teachings are universal."\\n—Basri Ket', '"There is no age at which you stop learning."', '"There\'s nothing quite as satisfying as delivering a good kick to the face."\\n—Adrasteia, Akroan captain', '"These terms are acceptable to House Dimir. Shall we shake on it?"', '"This arm\'s got plenty of use left in it. Who\'d throw such a nice thing away?"', '"Through the blood of the wicked, we shall be redeemed. Let us pray."', '"We\'ll pay no more tribute to that tyrannical lizard. A new age starts today!"\\n—Mayor Kadrim, now deceased', '"We\'re all food for something in the end."\\n—Cevraya, Golgari shaman', '"We\'re done here."', '"What did you catch today, my pet? Ah, it looks like a bit of vampire stuck between your teeth."\\n—Atla Palani, nest tender', '"What is this that is neither future nor past?"', '"What wishes do they grant? Mostly pinching-related ones."\\n—Omik, superintendent of waterworks', '"Wherever the strong would harm the weak, I will be there."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"Yes, nature is stronger. You don\'t see little buildings sprouting on trees."\\n—Emmara', '"You don\'t survive in the wild by standing in plain sight."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"You hit like a kobold!"', '"You know it\'s a great show when the Azorius arrest the props, too!"\\n—Judith, the Scourge Diva', '"You were so eager to take and consume. Yet when asked to give, you refuse?"', '"You\'re not setting foot in here. Not on our watch!"', '"Your crops will rot. The air itself will turn against you. You will suffer as I have suffered."\\n—Karaz, outcast', '"Your eyes aren\'t playing tricks on you. I am."', 'A unicorn chooses only the most virtuous and noble of knights to be its companion.', 'All seeds share a common bond, calling to each other across infinity.', "An aven's gear is enchanted to avoid weighing them down during aerial maneuvers.", 'An untroubled mind\\nDwells in perfect harmony\\nWith a peaceful heart.', "As blood touched the empty page, it formed words that seared themselves into the wizard's mind.", 'As the blaze raced toward her, Syr Ameril closed her eyes and pictured Castle Ardenvale so her last thoughts would be of home.', "Basri carries on his god's legacy, spreading her teachings throughout the Multiverse.", "Bedbugs aren't the only things you need to worry about biting you at night.", 'Being trapped between two forms of unlife is a fate worse than mere death.', "Beneath bright blossoms\\nVerdant with spring's rich bounty,\\nThe soul blooms in song.", "Charts and instruments work fine, but the best navigators aren't above a spell or two to nudge the tides in a more favorable direction.", 'Common Gruul career aspirations: berserker, shaman, catapult.', 'Dogs beg. Cats lay claim.', "Dominaria's most extravagant crypt nevertheless holds an empty grave.", 'Emphatic words with powerful gestures. Clearly this was playtime.', 'Even its shadow is a dazzling rainbow.', "Explosions aren't necessarily failures, just a different kind of success.", 'Fishing boats often follow hunting drakes to find the largest schools of fish.', 'For hydras, most problems can be solved with the addition of a few extra heads.', 'Freed from their respective labs, the two weirds formed a partnership, feeding on the arcane energies of war.', 'From here, the path to anywhere may be found.', 'Great evil weighs on the soul.', 'Great literature can transport the reader.', 'He became elder shaman when his predecessor was mysteriously struck by lightning on a cloudless day.', 'He will be your loyal champion, and his pack your protectors. All he asks for is a full belly, a spot by the fire, and all the love in your heart.', 'Her footsteps are whispers, her passage a last breath.', 'If a tree fells you in the forest and no one is around to hear it, "does it make a sound" is the last thing you need to worry about.', "If you feel the ground quake, run. If you hear its bellow, flee. If you see its teeth, it's too late.", "If you're lucky, the centaurs will give a single warning to leave their territory before driving a spear into you. If you're unlucky, the spear is the warning.", 'In dire times, even a place of refuge can become a weapon of war.', 'In nature, not a single bone or scrap of flesh goes to waste.', 'In the cloudy skies and dim light of autumn, a flash of white wings is a reminder that better times lie ahead.', "It cares more about preserving the herd's territory than about preserving itself.", 'It spins its web throughout the undercity, strange growths sprouting in its wake.', 'It was built to withstand the ages, but no one remembers who built it or why it keeps its eternal watch.', "It's often mistaken for the coming dawn as it gallops across the horizon.", "It's the favored mount of military commanders as well as anyone with a flair for the dramatic.", 'Its exploits are the stuff of legends among local chefs and fuel for nightmares among the forest thallids.', 'Its spark is worse than its bite.', 'Klothys set out to mend the destiny of Theros, her fury guiding every stitch.', 'Liliana inspires horror in many and fanatical admiration in a few.', "Lost at sea doesn't have to mean lost forever.", 'Many an inventor has collapsed under the pressure to create a flawless design.', 'Many names and many memories bound together in grim purpose.', "Might doesn't make right, but it does win the fight.", 'Nature\'s way of saying "take the long way home."', 'No one is as dedicated to perfection as a stitcher working on their latest masterpiece.', 'On the open sea, there is nowhere to hide.', 'One who is marked by a demon in life is sure to be remembered as one in death.', 'Rage smolders within,\\nAn all-consuming wildfire\\nBurning fear to ash', 'Rakdos cultists are her best customers. They never flinch at pain and are seldom good at math.', 'Renounce all limits,\\nFalse chains binding potential.\\nPower knows no bounds.', 'Resistance is unthinkable.', 'Rumors swirl of a pair of deadly Golgari assassins known only as the Left and Right Hands of the Ochran.', 'Scents fade and footprints wash away, but some trails can never be erased.', "Seeing it coming a mile away is little comfort if you can't get out of range in time.", 'Servants at Vess Manor are chosen for their strong work ethic and respectful demeanor. Being alive is not required.', 'She raised him from an orphaned pup and gave him a life of love. With his last act, he thanked her.', 'Some angels protect the meek and innocent. Others seek out and smite evil wherever it lurks.', "Some dogs just aren't meant to be indoor pets.", 'Some protection requires a bit of finesse.', 'Some who die senseless deaths return as formless spirits, seeking answers where there are none.', 'Sometimes knowledge takes on a life of its own.', "Teferi's legacy lives on in Tolaria through the study of time magic and a tradition of irrepressible mischief.", "The Blessed Sleep doesn't come easily to a mind chained by regrets.", 'The Vodalian Empire tends to be insular. The scholarly Volshe caste are the exception, using education as an antidote to xenophobia.', 'The best recipes start with reliable cookware.', "The crystal pulsed with the power of Teferi's Planeswalker spark. Had Jhoira given him a blessing or a curse?", 'The elves of Llanowar look to their past to determine the shape of their future.', "The forest's cover offers shade, shelter, and an increased risk of sudden death.", 'The hunt ends. Lunch begins.', 'The ingenuity of goblins, the depravity of demons, and the smarts of sheep.', 'The light washed over him, and in the wind he heard the roars of all the pridemates who had come before.', 'The mage scowled as yet another bolt splashed harmlessly against seemingly empty air.', 'The massive dominate through might. The tiny survive with guile. Beware the tiny who become massive.', 'The municipal senate makes extensive use of the thopters, mostly to gather dirt on rival senators.', 'The myr are like the Glimmervoid: blank canvases on which to build grand creations.', 'The ogres you know are nothing like the Onakke. Possessing both intellect and industry, they had brute strength without being brutish.', "The problem wasn't that fish had learned how to fly. It was that sharks had adapted to follow them.", "The purple banner of the House of Vess is a symbol of death wherever it's flown.", "The shaman looked at the world through Ghalta's eyes and understood that everything else was his prey.", 'The shaman rattles not to inspire a battle fury but to drown out the shrieks of those fleeing the Eldrazi.', 'The songs of angels are perceived not as words in the ears but as stirrings in the soul.', "Their ranks are thin, their formation is improvised, their weapons are borrowed, and you'd best get out of their way.", 'There are still places where a smile and a handshake are all you need to seal a deal.', 'There was no witty retort, no confident boast to accompany the attack. There was only pain.', 'Those who only believe themselves infected with lycanthropy can be as dangerous as those who really are.', 'To survive imminent doom, it sometimes takes a foolhardy soul who acts first and fears later.', 'To the Rakdos, screams of delight and screams of terror are one and the same.', 'Truth lurks in the depths,\\nInvisible from the shore.\\nKnowledge inundates.', 'Visitors marvel at its design, unaware of the other world that inspired it.', 'Weak and strong alike seek shelter beneath its branches.', 'Welcome to the club.', 'What the rangers thought were warning growls turned out to be nothing but monstrous snoring.', "When griffins started nesting atop the northern tower, the castellan worried they'd be a nuisance. Instead, they took the entire castle under their protection.", 'Who would you trust to watch your back more than yourself?', 'With great power comes great risk of getting yourself killed.', 'Within her battalion she was known as the Angel of Arkvale. Until now, that was only a metaphor.']
